WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
Hi I'm Florence Rose, I'm a model and a
makeup artist. If you want to find out

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:10.650
how to create this fresh, dewy makeup
look then keep watching. So first of all

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:15.089
I like to prime my face and I'm using
Ciaté's dewy spritz. I'm just taking

00:00:15.089 --> 00:00:19.619
this and doing a light spritz all over
my face and fanning it to make sure that

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:23.910
it's dry. Then moving on to base I'm
using makeup Forever's Ultra HD

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:28.619
Perfector. This is great for my skin tone
as it matches perfectly and it's really

00:00:28.619 --> 00:00:33.960
good to create a dewy natural look. I'm
dotting this all over my face to map out

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:38.579
the areas I want to cover and then using
a brush I'm blending this out initially

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:43.680
then taking slightly more putting under
my eye and blending this out with a small

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:48.350
Beauty Blender just to cover those dark
circles.

00:00:51.379 --> 00:00:55.949
Next moving on to blush, I like to use a
cream blusher and this is the CYO

00:00:55.949 --> 00:01:01.050
cosmetics in shade storyteller. I like to
use a cream blush because it's creamier

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:05.400
and a more natural look. I'm applying
this along my cheekbones and on the

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.790
apples of my cheeks slightly and across
the top of my nose to create a more

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:14.009
natural sunkissed blush. So to get more
warmth on the face I'm using the Laura

00:01:14.009 --> 00:01:18.570
Mercier Bronzer I'm just taking an
angled brush and applying this along my

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:23.009
cheekbones, along with bringing it up
towards my forehead and slightly around

00:01:23.009 --> 00:01:26.490
my jaw as this is the areas that the sun
will hit making it look like a natural

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:33.990
tan. Now for highlight I'm using Makeup
Forever's liquid highlighter, I really

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:38.610
love this highlighter as it's very
pearlescent, very natural-looking and goes

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:42.750
nicely with the blush and my pink hair.
I'm taking this and putting on the back

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:47.970
of my hand then using my finger to apply
to my cheekbone, along my brow bone, the

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:53.340
tip of my nose, the arch of my nose and
also along the Cupid's bow as I like to

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:56.090
wear a lot of highlight.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:02.520
And then to add a little sparkle and
make it quite festival wearable, I'm

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.410
taking Lime Crime Diamond Dew using the
brush that comes with, applying this to

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:11.880
my lid and blending out of my finger. I
love this product as it's very easy but

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:16.280
gives you a glam and ready to go look.

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.910
For lips I'm using NYX's dura chromatic
shimmer lip gloss in shade 'Spring It

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.320
On'. This is a great product, it's a lovely
colour and it catches highlights and

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.370
gives a gold shimmer to your lip. So
lastly I'm adding some fake freckles

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:37.260
using two products. One: the Kiko Milano
eyebrow marker in shade three which is

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:43.050
slightly darker also the Laura Mercier
bronzer in shade two with more of a warm

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:47.550
tone. I like to add freckles as it gives
more of a natural sunkissed look, almost

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:50.810
like you're wearing no makeup.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:03:06.550
For more videos like this subscribe to
GLAMOUR UK's YouTube channel.

